-- The vocabulary every discovery name table starts with.
---
Spellings seeded into every discovery name table, in this exact order, so
their `NameId`s are pinned: index `i` of this list is the id of its spelling
in every table discovery builds.

This is a copy of the existing compiler's whole synthesized vocabulary
(`name_table_synthesized_spellings` in `compiler/stage_02_lex/name_table.brp`),
kept in the same order so the ids agree when the legacy adapter hands these
tables' name table to the existing compiler's later phases, which compare ids
against that vocabulary's pinned `NAME_ID_*` constants;
`test_discovery_adapter` asserts the two lists are equal. It holds every
keyword spelling, the names the parser and later phases synthesize, the builtin
callees subscript lowering names, the foreign block argument names, the first
sixteen tuple field positions and the standard-library names later phases look
up.
---
SEEDED_NAME_SPELLINGS: List[String] = [
	"",
	"func",
	"pure",
	"var",
	"union",
	"record",
	"void",
	"while",
	"for",
	"in",
	"if",
